  "descriptions": {
    "preferred": "other The leaf shape of this cultivar is almost identical to that of 'Hagoromo'. However, the primary difference is in the variegated coloration. The leaf is occasionally whiteflecked with cream-colored irregular spots. It is not a strong color variegation, nor does it appear on all the leaves. If the plant is too vigorous or too highly fertilized, the variegations are masked for a growth period or two. Every effort should be made to keep the plant in good vigor but not overstimulated. It is not as strong growing as the non-variegated forms"
  },
